WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.286
Welcome. This class shows how to observe
an agent system

2
00:00:04.286 --> 00:00:08.571
without turning telemetry into an
uncontrolled copy of user data.

3
00:00:08.571 --> 00:00:12.857
You will connect causal spans, measure
useful outcomes, minimize sensitive

4
00:00:12.857 --> 00:00:17.143
content, diagnose the first wrong
transition, repair one deterministic

5
00:00:17.143 --> 00:00:21.429
privacy defect, and prepare a
decision-ready human escalation. The

6
00:00:21.429 --> 00:00:25.714
examples are synthetic. A passing exercise
is not evidence that

7
00:00:25.714 --> 00:00:30.000
a production system is instrumented
safely.

8
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.333
Use traces, metrics, logs, and evaluations
together because each answers

9
00:00:34.333 --> 00:00:38.667
a different question. A trace reconstructs
one run and its

10
00:00:38.667 --> 00:00:43.000
parent-child operations. Metrics reveal
trends, distributions, and service

11
00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:47.333
objectives across many runs. Logs record
discrete operational events. Evaluations

12
00:00:47.333 --> 00:00:51.667
judge behavior against an explicit rubric.
None replaces the others.

13
00:00:51.667 --> 00:00:56.000
Begin with a decision the team must make.
Perhaps you

14
00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:00.333
need to detect a regression, locate a
failed boundary, control

15
00:01:00.333 --> 00:01:04.667
spend, explain an escalation, or prove
that a postcondition held.

16
00:01:04.667 --> 00:01:09.000
Collect only signals that support a named
decision, control, or

17
00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:13.333
obligation. A quality metric can show that
successful completion declined

18
00:01:13.333 --> 00:01:17.667
after a workflow release, but it cannot
localize the retrieval,

19
00:01:17.667 --> 00:01:22.000
approval, or tool boundary that failed in
one run. A

20
00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:26.333
trace can localize that run. An evaluation
can judge whether

21
00:01:26.333 --> 00:01:30.667
the final behavior met the task rubric. A
log can

22
00:01:30.667 --> 00:01:35.000
record that an escalation packet was
created. Request volume alone

23
00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:39.333
is not an outcome, and a full transcript
alone is

24
00:01:39.333 --> 00:01:43.667
not aggregate reliability. Also remember
the boundary of this lesson.

25
00:01:43.667 --> 00:01:48.000
The lab uses deterministic JSON fixtures.
It does not prove

26
00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:52.333
that a deployed system creates spans at
real workflow boundaries,

27
00:01:52.333 --> 00:01:56.667
propagates identifiers across external
calls, or exports genuine provider and

28
00:01:56.667 --> 00:02:01.000
tool outcomes.

29
00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:05.450
Preserve causal structure across the run.
Give the workflow a

30
00:02:05.450 --> 00:02:09.900
trace identifier. Give each agent step,
model call, retrieval, tool

31
00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:14.350
call, approval, handoff, verifier, and
recovery step a span with

32
00:02:14.350 --> 00:02:18.800
its own identifier, parent linkage,
timing, status, and failure class.

33
00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:23.250
Record stable references to workflow,
prompt, model, tool, policy, and

34
00:02:23.250 --> 00:02:27.700
content versions. A portable span envelope
includes the trace identifier,

35
00:02:27.700 --> 00:02:32.150
span identifier, parent identifier,
operation, version references, start and

36
00:02:32.150 --> 00:02:36.600
end times, status, failure class, usage,
retries, estimated cost, and

37
00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:41.050
a redacted evidence reference. Use
low-cardinality fields such as operation

38
00:02:41.050 --> 00:02:45.500
type and terminal state for aggregation.
Keep detailed evidence behind

39
00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:49.950
access-controlled references. A span
contract says what must be true

40
00:02:49.950 --> 00:02:54.400
before and after an operation. Preparation
may produce a non-executing

41
00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:58.850
action plan. Approval may authorize or
deny it. Verification may

42
00:02:58.850 --> 00:03:03.300
confirm that no side effect occurred after
denial. Status alone

43
00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:07.750
is not enough. Record a compact outcome
such as prepared,

44
00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:12.200
denied, recovered, escalated, or verified
no effect. Correlation identifiers can

45
00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:16.650
connect provider requests and external
effects, but they must be

46
00:03:16.650 --> 00:03:21.100
random or otherwise non-semantic. Do not
put an email address,

47
00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:25.550
account number, customer name, prompt
text, or sensitive value in

48
00:03:25.550 --> 00:03:30.000
an identifier or metric label.

49
00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:34.357
Measure outcomes, not activity alone.
Track task success and verified

50
00:03:34.357 --> 00:03:38.714
completion beside policy violations,
unsafe attempts, user corrections,

51
00:03:38.714 --> 00:03:43.071
escalations, abandonment, tool and
retrieval failures, retries, latency,

52
00:03:43.071 --> 00:03:47.429
token use, and cost per successful task.
Segment these measures

53
00:03:47.429 --> 00:03:51.786
by workflow version, model, tool, user
journey, risk class, language,

54
00:03:51.786 --> 00:03:56.143
and other supported groups. Define every
metric before graphing it.

55
00:03:56.143 --> 00:04:00.500
Outcome says what happened to the task.
Quality compares behavior

56
00:04:00.500 --> 00:04:04.857
with a rubric. Safety records attempted
and prevented violations separately.

57
00:04:04.857 --> 00:04:09.214
Reliability records whether required
boundaries completed and whether recovery

58
00:04:09.214 --> 00:04:13.571
restored a valid state. Escalation records
both the trigger and

59
00:04:13.571 --> 00:04:17.929
whether a human decision was requested.
State whether token and

60
00:04:17.929 --> 00:04:22.286
cost fields are provider-reported, locally
counted, or estimated. For the

61
00:04:22.286 --> 00:04:26.643
supplied fixture, use nearest rank across
all eight spans, including

62
00:04:26.643 --> 00:04:31.000
the root agent span. The ordered latency
values are 15,

63
00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:35.357
20, 25, 30, 40, 60, 120, and 900
milliseconds. The

64
00:04:35.357 --> 00:04:39.714
fourth value is the nearest rank for eight
observations at

65
00:04:39.714 --> 00:04:44.071
the fiftieth percentile, so p50 is 30
milliseconds. The nearest

66
00:04:44.071 --> 00:04:48.429
rank for the ninety-fifth percentile is
the eighth value, so

67
00:04:48.429 --> 00:04:52.786
p95 is 900 milliseconds. These are
exercise results, not production

68
00:04:52.786 --> 00:04:57.143
objectives. The exercise cost convention
is 0.001 dollars per token.

69
00:04:57.143 --> 00:05:01.500
The model span has 180 input tokens plus
40 output

70
00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:05.857
tokens, for 220 total tokens. Multiply
0.001 by 220: the

71
00:05:05.857 --> 00:05:10.214
estimated cost is 0.220 dollars. This is a
local exercise

72
00:05:10.214 --> 00:05:14.571
estimate, not a provider invoice. Any
clear-text approval argument is

73
00:05:14.571 --> 00:05:18.929
an immediate privacy alert in this
exercise. An action after

74
00:05:18.929 --> 00:05:23.286
denial is an immediate safety alert. An
unknown final verification

75
00:05:23.286 --> 00:05:27.643
enters human escalation. Product owners
must select real thresholds from

76
00:05:27.643 --> 00:05:32.000
representative traffic.

77
00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:36.450
Assume model and tool content is
sensitive. Inputs, outputs, retrieval

78
00:05:36.450 --> 00:05:40.900
queries, documents, tool arguments,
results, and approval notes may contain

79
00:05:40.900 --> 00:05:45.350
personal data, secrets, customer content,
or protected business information. Default

80
00:05:45.350 --> 00:05:49.800
to metadata and secure references. The
lesson default exports operation

81
00:05:49.800 --> 00:05:54.250
names, opaque identifiers, version
references, status, duration, aggregate

82
00:05:54.250 --> 00:05:58.700
token counts, estimated cost, and redacted
field-name summaries. It does

83
00:05:58.700 --> 00:06:03.150
not export full prompts, hidden reasoning,
credentials, raw retrieval documents,

84
00:06:03.150 --> 00:06:07.600
argument values, or result bodies. A
complete telemetry policy answers

85
00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:12.050
eight questions. What purpose requires
each field? What redaction runs

86
00:06:12.050 --> 00:06:16.500
before export? Which approved population,
if any, permits content capture?

87
00:06:16.500 --> 00:06:20.950
What risk-based sampling rule selects
runs? Which role may read

88
00:06:20.950 --> 00:06:25.400
each data class? When is each class
removed? How does

89
00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:29.850
subject or tenant deletion propagate to
telemetry and backups? Which

90
00:06:29.850 --> 00:06:34.300
approved region permits collection,
processing, and storage? Apply redaction

91
00:06:34.300 --> 00:06:38.750
before export, isolate tenants, encrypt
data, enforce role-based access, audit

92
00:06:38.750 --> 00:06:43.200
access, use short retention, propagate
deletion, and apply regional controls.

93
00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:47.650
Sample because of risk and debugging need,
not merely because

94
00:06:47.650 --> 00:06:52.100
storage is available. Synthetic canaries
can test leakage. Never insert

95
00:06:52.100 --> 00:06:56.550
a real secret to test redaction.
Observability that violates the

96
00:06:56.550 --> 00:07:01.000
product's data promises is an operational
failure.

97
00:07:01.000 --> 00:07:05.474
Begin at the user-visible failure, then
walk backward to the

98
00:07:05.474 --> 00:07:09.947
first span whose actual state diverged
from its expected contract.

99
00:07:09.947 --> 00:07:14.421
Compare input, output, authority,
postcondition, and state at each boundary.

100
00:07:14.421 --> 00:07:18.895
Classify the first divergence before
changing a prompt. Possible classes

101
00:07:18.895 --> 00:07:23.368
include model, prompt, tool, retrieval,
data, policy, infrastructure, and

102
00:07:23.368 --> 00:07:27.842
orchestration. Escalate when the trace
indicates an unsafe action, cross-tenant

103
00:07:27.842 --> 00:07:32.316
data, repeated unknown outcomes, policy
conflict, or impact beyond automated

104
00:07:32.316 --> 00:07:36.789
recovery. Give the human a redacted
timeline, affected targets, containment

105
00:07:36.789 --> 00:07:41.263
status, evidence references, confirmed
facts, remaining uncertainty, and the

106
00:07:41.263 --> 00:07:45.737
exact decision required. Do not include
secrets, unnecessary customer content,

107
00:07:45.737 --> 00:07:50.211
unsupported blame, or hidden reasoning.
For this synthetic case, the

108
00:07:50.211 --> 00:07:54.684
packet identifies trace tr demo seven,
workflow version wf three,

109
00:07:54.684 --> 00:07:59.158
and a synthetic account target. The issue
is clear-text approval

110
00:07:59.158 --> 00:08:03.632
arguments in telemetry. Containment is to
disable the affected exporter

111
00:08:03.632 --> 00:08:08.105
route and restrict trace access. The
verified workflow effect is

112
00:08:08.105 --> 00:08:12.579
no external action. Evidence references
are the approval span and

113
00:08:12.579 --> 00:08:17.053
verifier span. The requested decision is
to authorize a redacted

114
00:08:17.053 --> 00:08:21.526
re-export and deletion of the defective
record. The packet excludes

115
00:08:21.526 --> 00:08:26.000
full prompts, hidden reasoning, and
argument values.

116
00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:30.333
A support agent claims a policy exception.
The final model

117
00:08:30.333 --> 00:08:34.667
span looks fluent and the tool span
succeeded. Walking backward

118
00:08:34.667 --> 00:08:39.000
reveals that retrieval selected an expired
policy because the content-version

119
00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:43.333
filter was missing. The verifier checked
citation format but not

120
00:08:43.333 --> 00:08:47.667
effective date. Classify the first
divergence as retrieval or data

121
00:08:47.667 --> 00:08:52.000
freshness, not model style. Disable the
affected route, preserve the

122
00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:56.333
content and workflow version references,
add a dated-policy regression case,

123
00:08:56.333 --> 00:09:00.667
and give the reviewer a redacted timeline.
Changing temperature would

124
00:09:00.667 --> 00:09:05.000
not repair the failed boundary.

125
00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:09.000
Choose one raw telemetry field from an
agent workflow. State

126
00:09:09.000 --> 00:09:13.000
the operator decision it supports. Then
replace it with the

127
00:09:13.000 --> 00:09:17.000
least sensitive metadata, classification,
hash, or secure reference that still

128
00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:21.000
supports that decision. Include who may
access it, how long

129
00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:25.000
it is retained, and how deletion reaches
backups. Do not

130
00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:29.000
use a real secret or personal data in your

131
00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:33.000
answer.

132
00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:07.667
Checkpoint. Should a human escalation
packet include full customer prompts

133
00:11:07.667 --> 00:11:12.333
and hidden model reasoning by default so
the reviewer has

134
00:11:12.333 --> 00:11:17.000
every detail? Pause and decide before
hearing the explanation.

135
00:12:17.000 --> 00:12:21.000
No. The default packet contains a redacted
timeline, affected targets,

136
00:12:21.000 --> 00:12:25.000
versions, containment, evidence
references, uncertainty, and the required

137
00:12:25.000 --> 00:12:29.000
decision. Include content only when
purpose, permission, access, retention,

138
00:12:29.000 --> 00:12:33.000
and deletion policy justify it. Hidden
reasoning is not required

139
00:12:33.000 --> 00:12:37.000
for operational accountability. If you
chose full capture for convenience,

140
00:12:37.000 --> 00:12:41.000
return to data minimization. If you
removed every detail, restore

141
00:12:41.000 --> 00:12:45.000
enough governed evidence to understand the
state transition and decide

142
00:12:45.000 --> 00:12:49.000
containment or recovery.

143
00:12:49.000 --> 00:12:53.000
Open the trace review activity. Create a
schema for agent,

144
00:12:53.000 --> 00:12:57.000
model, retrieval, tool, approval, handoff,
verification, and recovery spans. Define

145
00:12:57.000 --> 00:13:01.000
quality, safety, reliability, latency,
token, cost, and escalation metrics with

146
00:13:01.000 --> 00:13:05.000
